Name: quic_use_ebpf
Type: SWITCH
Default-Value: 0
Last-Modified: UNRELEASED

Whether to use eBPF-based kernel steering to dispatch proto="quic"
connections (see master/quic/quic_ebpf.c), when this build has that support
compiled in. Off by default, because master must retain CAP_BPF,
CAP_NET_ADMIN and CAP_PERFMON for its whole life to load and attach the
steering program: that is worth opting into, not something a deployment
should acquire merely by installing a build that happens to have eBPF
support. Left off, master uses its userspace relay-based dispatch instead
(see master/quic/quic_relay.c), which needs no elevated privileges but
relays every packet of a connection rather than just the first. Has no
effect on a build without eBPF support at all, which always uses the
userspace relay regardless of this setting.
